{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785175412396,"sessionID":"ses_05b4ae99bffebcntbfleru5bq2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_sKZrJCHOxi7u5xigwK5rDmei","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","limit":500},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy: Root-Level Skill Metadata JSON Contract\n2: \n3: ## 2. TOPIC\n4: Establish the consumer-derived contract for root-level metadata JSON files across all 12 `.opencode/skills/` roots, without inspecting nested packet/mode metadata as fleet members and without conflating skill metadata with spec-folder continuity metadata.\n5: \n6: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n7: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n8: - [x] What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n9: - [ ] What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n10: - [ ] What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n11: - [ ] How should the five graph-only skills, `leaf-aliases.json`, `command-metadata.json`, and sparse `sk-git` be classified after behavior-impact checks?\n12: - [ ] Where should the canonical contract live in `sk-doc/create-skill`, what can be generated/backfilled, and what fleet-wide presence-plus-freshness gate should enforce it?\n13: \n14: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n15: \n16: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n17: - Do not implement or backfill metadata.\n18: - Do not treat nested mode/packet JSON as fleet root metadata.\n19: - Do not conflate `.opencode/skills/**/{description,graph-metadata}.json` with `.opencode/specs/**` continuity schemas.\n20: - Do not modify researched source files.\n21: \n22: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n23: - Stop at 10 iterations.\n24: - Stop earlier only after at least three evidence iterations, all five key questions are evidence-backed, the census covers all 12 skills and eight file types, disputed cases are resolved, and citations cover producers, consumers, schemas, and tests.\n25: \n26: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n27: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n28: - What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n29: \n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n31: \n32: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n33: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n34: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n35: - exact direct-child globbing produced a scope-safe census without admitting nested packet metadata; focused source reads then separated scaffold outputs, generated artifacts, and authored inputs. (iteration 1)\n36: \n37: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n38: \n39: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n40: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n41: - broad `command-metadata.json` search output was too large because repository-wide references include large records; narrowed producer searches were clean but yielded only negative evidence. (iteration 1)\n42: \n43: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n44: \n45: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n46: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n47: ### A broad `command-metadata.json` search produced oversized output; narrowing to the create-command and command trees found no producer. Future work should search its consumers and Git history rather than repeat the broad search. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n48: - What was tried: A broad `command-metadata.json` search produced oversized output; narrowing to the create-command and command trees found no producer. Future work should search its consumers and Git history rather than repeat the broad search.\n49: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n50: - Do NOT retry: A broad `command-metadata.json` search produced oversized output; narrowing to the create-command and command trees found no producer. Future work should search its consumers and Git history rather than repeat the broad search.\n51: \n52: ### Counting `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `tsconfig.json`: they are root JSON files but not among the eight named metadata types. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n53: - What was tried: Counting `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `tsconfig.json`: they are root JSON files but not among the eight named metadata types.\n54: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n55: - Do NOT retry: Counting `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `tsconfig.json`: they are root JSON files but not among the eight named metadata types.\n56: \n57: ### Counting nested mode/packet JSON: excluded by the focus contract and direct-child glob. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n58: - What was tried: Counting nested mode/packet JSON: excluded by the focus contract and direct-child glob.\n59: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n60: - Do NOT retry: Counting nested mode/packet JSON: excluded by the focus contract and direct-child glob.\n61: \n62: ### The similarly named root-name consumer-matrix test concerns catalog/playbook directory names, not this eight-file metadata census. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/tests/test-root-name-consumer-matrix.cjs:80-138] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n63: - What was tried: The similarly named root-name consumer-matrix test concerns catalog/playbook directory names, not this eight-file metadata census. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/tests/test-root-name-consumer-matrix.cjs:80-138]\n64: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n65: - Do NOT retry: