{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785176189517,"sessionID":"ses_05b4ae99bffebcntbfleru5bq2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_liYLM9vRJtRojoL6KB6BUmbo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/prompts/iteration-004.md\n+DEEP-RESEARCH\n+Resolved route: mode=research; target_agent=@deep-research; execution=single_iteration; state_source=externalized_files; do_not_switch_mode=true\n+\n+# Deep-Research Iteration 4\n+\n+## STATE\n+Segment: 1 | Iteration: 4 of 10\n+Questions: 2/5 answered | Last focus: remaining leaf/command metadata schemas and consumers\n+Last 2 ratios: 1.00 -> 1.00 | Stuck count: 0\n+Next focus: Derive the consumer-based skill taxonomy and resolve every exceptional presence case.\n+\n+## STATE FILES\n+- Config: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-config.json`\n+- State Log: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-state.jsonl`\n+- Strategy: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md`\n+- Registry: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/findings-registry.json`\n+- Prior evidence: packet iterations 1-3\n+- Write narrative: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md`\n+- Write delta: `.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deltas/iter-004.jsonl`\n+\n+## FOCUS\n+Derive the smallest skill CLASS TAXONOMY from actual consumer requirements, not current presence. Map all 12 skill roots onto classes and state each class's mandatory root file set. Reconcile every matrix difference as a class rule or named defect. Resolve with behavior evidence: why `mcp-code-mode`, `sk-git`, `system-code-graph`, `system-skill-advisor`, and `system-spec-kit` have graph metadata without description and whether adding description can change advisor scoring/routing; whether aliases stay authored; whether command metadata remains sk-design-specific or should generalize to command-owning `sk-doc`, `system-deep-loop`, and `system-spec-kit`; and whether `sk-git` is a legitimate sparse class or the fleet's most non-conforming root. Explicitly correct the phrase “five graph-only skills” if only `sk-git` is literally graph-only.\n+\n+## CONSTRAINTS\n+- Read state, registry, and iterations 1-3 first.\n+- Exactly one LEAF iteration; no subagents.\n+- 3-5 focused actions, max 12 tool calls.\n+- Findings only; do not modify metadata or run a write-mode backfill.\n+- Cite consumer/scorer behavior and each class mapping with precise file:line evidence or inference markers.\n+- Do not infer class solely from currently present files.\n+- Write only the narrative, append-only state log, and delta above.\n+- Mark taxonomy and exception key questions answered only if all 12 roots and all disputed cases are explicitly resolved.\n+\n+## OUTPUT CONTRACT\n+Create the narrative, append one canonical iteration record, and create the delta. Both require iteration/run 4, mode research, route proof, novelty/source fields, and cli-opencode model provenance.\n+The narrative must contain Focus, Actions Taken, Findings, a 12-root class mapping, per-class mandatory file sets, Defects, Ruled Out, Dead Ends, Sources Consulted, Assessment, Reflection, Questions Answered/Remaining, and Recommended Next Focus.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unificati