{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785176703187,"sessionID":"ses_05b4ae99bffebcntbfleru5bq2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_8Wtbv8Q2J9RKT5lYajnFpEK6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","offset":1,"limit":45},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy: Root-Level Skill Metadata JSON Contract\n2: \n3: ## 2. TOPIC\n4: Establish the consumer-derived contract for root-level metadata JSON files across all 12 `.opencode/skills/` roots, without inspecting nested packet/mode metadata as fleet members and without conflating skill metadata with spec-folder continuity metadata.\n5: \n6: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n7: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n8: - [x] What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n9: - [x] What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n10: - [x] What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n11: - [ ] How should the five graph-only skills, `leaf-aliases.json`, `command-metadata.json`, and sparse `sk-git` be classified after behavior-impact checks?\n12: - [ ] Where should the canonical contract live in `sk-doc/create-skill`, what can be generated/backfilled, and what fleet-wide presence-plus-freshness gate should enforce it?\n13: \n14: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n15: \n16: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n17: - Do not implement or backfill metadata.\n18: - Do not treat nested mode/packet JSON as fleet root metadata.\n19: - Do not conflate `.opencode/skills/**/{description,graph-metadata}.json` with `.opencode/specs/**` continuity schemas.\n20: - Do not modify researched source files.\n21: \n22: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n23: - Stop at 10 iterations.\n24: - Stop earlier only after at least three evidence iterations, all five key questions are evidence-backed, the census covers all 12 skills and eight file types, disputed cases are resolved, and citations cover producers, consumers, schemas, and tests.\n25: \n26: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n27: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n28: - What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n29: - What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n30: - What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n31: \n32: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n33: \n34: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n35: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n36: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n37: - exact direct-child globbing produced a scope-safe census without admitting nested packet metadata; focused source reads then separated scaffold outputs, generated artifacts, and authored inputs. (iteration 1)\n38: - owner-scoped searches followed by implementation reads separated real file reads from thousands of continuity/docs mentions and exposed the direct-versus-indirect advisor boundary. (iteration 2)\n39: - executable-extension searches avoided the blocked prose/spec noise, while owner-focused reads exposed direct versus indirect consumers and the file-versus-surface cardinality distinction. (iteration 3)\n40: - consumer obligations reduced eight presence columns to two classes plus narrow overlays, allowing the census to expose defects rather than define classes. (iteration 4)\n41: \n42: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n43: \n44: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n45: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n(Showing lines 1-45 of 216. Use offset=46 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Research Strategy: Root-Level Skill Metadata JSON Contract\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nEstablish the consumer-derived contract for root-level metadata JSON files across all 12 `.opencode/skills/` roots, without inspecting nested packet/mode metadata as fleet members and without conflating skill metadata with spec-folder continuity metadata.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n- [x] What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n- [x] What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n- [ ] How should the five graph-only skills, `leaf-aliases.json`, `command-metadata.json`, and sparse `sk-git` be classified after behavior-impact checks?\n- [ ] Where should the canonical contract live in `sk-doc/create-skill`, what can be generated/backfilled, and what fleet-wide presence-plus-freshness gate should enforce it?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Do not implement or backfill metadata.\n- Do not treat nested mode/packet JSON as fleet root metadata.\n- Do not conflate `.opencode/skills/**/{description,graph-metadata}.json` with `.opencode/specs/**` continuity schemas.\n- Do not modify researched source files.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Research Strategy: Root-Level Skill Metadata JSON Contract\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nEstablish the consumer-derived contract for root-level metadata JSON files across all 12 `.opencode/skills/` roots, without inspecting nested packet/mode metadata as fleet members and without conflating skill metadata with spec-folder continuity metadata.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n- [x] What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n- [x] What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n- [ ] How should the five graph-only skills, `leaf-aliases.json`, `command-metadata.json`, and sparse `sk-git` be classified after behavior-impact checks?\n- [ ] Where should the canonical contract live in `sk-doc/create-skill`, what can be generated/backfilled, and what fleet-wide presence-plus-freshness gate should enforce it?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Do not implement or backfill metadata.\n- Do not treat nested mode/packet JSON as fleet root metadata.\n- Do not conflate `.opencode/skills/**/{description,graph-metadata}.json` with `.opencode/specs/**` continuity schemas.\n- Do not modify researched source files.\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Stop at 10 iterations.\n- Stop earlier only after at least three evidence iterations, all five key questions are evidence-backed, the census covers all 12 skills and eight file types, disputed cases are resolved, and citations cover producers, consumers, schemas, and tests.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n- What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n- What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n- What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n- exact direct-child globbing produced a scope-safe census without admitting nested packet metadata; focused source reads then separated scaffold outputs, generated artifacts, and authored inputs. (iteration 1)\n- owner-scoped searches followed by implementation reads separated real file reads from thousands of continuity/docs mentions and exposed the direct-versus-indirect advisor boundary. (iteration 2)\n- executable-extension searches avoided the blocked prose/spec noise, while owner-focused reads exposed direct versus indirect consumers and the file-versus-surface cardinality distinction. (iteration 3)\n- consumer obligations reduced eight presence columns to two classes plus narrow overlays, allowing the census to expose defects rather than define classes. (iteration 4)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":45,"totalLines":216,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1785176703180,"end":1785176703186}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d3b7521e193a323016a67a27e0fdc8191adf4b1dd5082c539"}},"id":"prt_fa4d2bcb4001PbH2LQpP4gNytI","sessionID":"ses_05b4ae99bffebcntbfleru5bq2","messageID":"msg_fa4d2a1280010Co0MBRysJsFBa"}}
