{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785177351480,"sessionID":"ses_05b4ae99bffebcntbfleru5bq2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_o0mmkW3fExHGicysjnZ65Esr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"17-section|## 17\\.|## 16\\.|Eliminated Alternatives","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research"},"output":"Found 22 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/synthesis-save-and-guardrails/ruled-out-directions-in-synthesis.md:\n  Line 3: description: \"Verify that iteration ruledOut data is consolidated into an Eliminated Alternatives section in research/research.md.\"\n\n  Line 15: This scenario validates that ruled-out directions are properly synthesized for `DR-026`. The objective is to verify that `ruledOut` data from iteration JSONL records and `## Dead Ends` sections from iteration files are consolidated into a mandatory \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section in `research/research.md`.\n\n  Line 27: - Objective: Verify that iteration ruledOut data is consolidated into \"Eliminated Alternatives\" in research/research.md.\n\n  Line 32: - Expected signals: research/research.md has a mandatory \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section formatted as a table (`| Approach | Reason Eliminated | Evidence | Iteration(s) |`); iteration files have `## Ruled Out` and `## Dead Ends` sections when negative knowledge is captured; strategy.md has a `## 10. Ruled Out Directions` section updated per iteration; ALWAYS rule 10 mandates documenting ruled-out directions.\n\n  Line 33: - Pass/fail posture: PASS if the synthesis phase produces an \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section in research/research.md consolidating all ruledOut and Dead Ends data, and the upstream sources (JSONL, iteration files, strategy.md) consistently feed this section; FAIL if the section is missing, data is not consolidated, or upstream sources lack the required fields.\n\n  Line 48: 1. `bash: rg -n 'Eliminated Alternatives\\|ruledOut\\|Dead Ends\\|negative knowledge' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md`\n\n  Line 53: research/research.md has mandatory \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section as a table; iteration files have `## Ruled Out` and `## Dead Ends` sections; strategy.md has `## 10. Ruled Out Directions` section; JSONL records include `ruledOut` array; ALWAYS rule 10 mandates per-iteration documentation of ruled-out directions.\n\n  Line 55: Capture the loop protocol synthesis rules (Step 3 with Eliminated Alternatives), the state format ruledOut array schema and iteration file requirements, the strategy template Ruled Out Directions section, and SKILL.md ALWAYS rule 10.\n\n  Line 57: PASS if the synthesis phase produces an \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section in research/research.md consolidating all ruledOut and Dead Ends data, and upstream sources consistently feed this section; FAIL if the section is missing, data is not consolidated, or upstream sources lack the required fields.\n\n  Line 75: | `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md` | Loop protocol; inspect `ANCHOR:phase-synthesis` for the Eliminated Alternatives consolidation rules (synthesis Step 3) |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:\n  Line 670: Verify that iteration ruledOut data is consolidated into \"Eliminated Alternatives\" in research/research.md.\n\n  Line 673: Prompt summary: As a manual-testing orchestrator, validate the ruled-out directions synthesis contract for deep-research against the current deep-research docs, command entrypoint, YAML workflow, and runtime anchors. Verify the synthesis phase consolidates ruledOut entries from JSONL records and ## Dead Ends sections from iteration files into a mandatory \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section in research/research.md. Verify that strategy.md also tracks ruled-out directions per iteration. Return a concise operator-facing verdict.\n\n  Line 675: Expected signals: research/research.md has a mandatory \"Eliminated Alternatives\" section formatted as a table (`| Approach | Reason Eliminated | Evidence | Iteration(s) |`); iteration files have `## Ruled Out` and `## Dead Ends` sections when negative knowledge is captured; strategy.md has a `## 10. Ruled Out Directions` section updated per iteration; ALWAYS rule 10 mandates documenting ruled-out directions.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:\n  Line 86: Synthesis owns the final `research/research.md` output. It reads all iteration files and the final strategy state, compiles the standard 17-section research document, adds the required `Eliminated Alternatives` table, marks the config status complete, and appends a `synthesis_complete` event to the JSONL log.\n\n  Line 442: Iteration files include `Ruled Out` and `Dead Ends` sections, JSONL records can carry structured `ruledOut` entries, and the reducer promotes those failed paths into the strategy and findings registry. Final synthesis then consolidates them into the required `Eliminated Alternatives` section so later iterations and later readers do not repeat dead paths.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/loop-lifecycle/synthesis.md:\n  Line 27: The synthesis phase reads every iteration file plus the final strategy state, then writes the canonical `research/research.md` document in the standard 17-section format. This phase owns deduplication and final organization even when progressive synthesis has already been updating the file during earlier iterations.\n\n  Line 29: Negative knowledge is part of the live contract here. Synthesis must consolidate `ruledOut` entries and `Dead Ends` sections into a required `Eliminated Alternatives` table. It also updates the config status to `complete` and appends a `synthesis_complete` event so later tooling can tell the packet has reached terminal synthesis.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/research-output/progressive-synthesis.md:\n  Line 29: The final workflow still owns synthesis. After convergence, the synth phase reads all iteration files and the final strategy state, deduplicates overlap, and cleans the document into the canonical 17-section structure. If `progressiveSynthesis` is disabled, the loop skips iteration-time writes and creates `research/research.md` from scratch during synthesis, but the file remains the workflow-owned final research surface in both modes.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/feature-catalog/research-output/negative-knowledge.md:\n  Line 29: The reducer and synthesis phases keep that information alive. `reduce-state.cjs` promotes ruled-out directions into the strategy and findings registry so future iterations can avoid retrying blocked paths. Final synthesis then consolidates those eliminated paths into the required `Eliminated Alternatives` table inside `research/research.md`, which turns negative knowledge into a durable research output.\n\n  Line 41: | `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md` | Reference | Defines the `Eliminated Alternatives` synthesis contract. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:\n  Line 535: 3. **Compile research/research.md**: Merge findings into 17-section format\n\n  Line 542:    - **Include a mandatory \"## Eliminated Alternatives\" section** as primary research output:\n","metadata":{"matches":22,"truncated":false},"title":"17-section|## 17\\.|## 16\\.|Eliminated Alternatives","time":{"start":1785177351411,"end":1785177351478}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04388ef1d7afc60c016a67a50574b48191b61184b5f5cb301e"}},"id":"prt_fa4dc9d80001iWUJhozh3UdrRt","sessionID":"ses_05b4ae99bffebcntbfleru5bq2","messageID":"msg_fa4dc84170010A7AJZTbw9vlIT"}}
